Subject: [PATCH] backlight: tb371fc: unwind global state on probe failure

Each controller is linked into a global list before the initial
brightness writes. If one of those writes fails, probe returns an error
and devres frees the controller, but remove() is not called. A later
brightness update can then traverse a freed list node. If this probe also
registered the shared backlight, its global pointer becomes stale too.

Unlink the failed controller under the existing mutex on every failure
following list insertion. Clear the shared pointer only when it belongs
to this client, and clear client data. Keep the successfully bound peer
and any shared backlight owned by a different client. Fold registration
failure into the same cleanup so the list entry is removed exactly once.

The devm registration continues to own backlight unregistration; do not
unregister it a second time. Brightness values, sink masks, register writes
and successful probe/remove behavior are unchanged.

Apply to drivers/video/backlight/tb371fc-ktz8866.c after copying the
unmodified mainline-port/backports/linux-6.12/tb371fc-ktz8866.c into the
kernel tree. The same hunks also match the mainline-port/drivers source
and the historical scripts/r170-backlight source when staged at that path.

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/tb371fc-ktz8866.c b/drivers/video/backlight/tb371fc-ktz8866.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/tb371fc-ktz8866.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/tb371fc-ktz8866.c
@@ -121,7 +121,6 @@
 		if (IS_ERR(tb371fc_backlight)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(tb371fc_backlight);
 			tb371fc_backlight = NULL;
-			list_del(&ktz->node);
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -139,6 +138,14 @@
 		} else {
 			ret = tb371fc_ktz8866_write_level(ktz, brightness);
 		}
+	}
+	if (ret) {
+		/* Probe failure releases devres without calling remove(). */
+		list_del(&ktz->node);
+		if (tb371fc_backlight &&
+		    tb371fc_backlight->dev.parent == &client->dev)
+			tb371fc_backlight = NULL;
+		i2c_set_clientdata(client, NULL);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&tb371fc_ktz8866_lock);
 
